#
# The pinned k3ctl client (planning/mvp-m1-plan.md, "Tool lock and the
# clean evaluator" and "The remote reset"; Q14): the one client the board
# tools run for K3_RESET=k3ctl, as `/usr/bin/python3 -I -B CLIENT -d DEVICE
# COMMAND`, the locked Python 3 in isolated mode, with COMMAND only `status`
# or `reset` (the client itself pings first). k3ctl is not a lock role: it
# is a script in the
# responsible human's k3-com260-info checkout (tools/k3ctl/k3ctl) that no
# package owns and the evaluator never runs. tools/k3-run.sh, which
# tools/k3-campaign.sh asks before any run, refuses a K3CTL whose SHA-256
# differs from sha256 below, or a K3CTL or K3CTL_DEV not of the forms
# below (stop condition 10), before any run and again before each
# command; tools/k3-preflight.sh records the comparison. The value is the
# client's SHA-256 the plan recorded at planning time (2026-10-26), found
# unchanged in that checkout at M1-5 (2026-10-27). Change it only on the
# responsible human's direction, after reviewing the new client.
#
#   sha256   the client's SHA-256
#   client   the form K3CTL must have: an absolute path of these characters
#   device   the form K3CTL_DEV must have: a path under /dev
sha256=7ca3d78a47de404becc6ee8450617dfad4382b7e316e37370f203be6e7eea3ec
client=^/[A-Za-z0-9._+/-]+$
device=^/dev/[A-Za-z0-9._+/-]+$
